WEBVTT

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.150
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:31.070
<i>The Nautilus was trapped by the mysterious Neo Atlanteans,</i>

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:36.950
<i>and sank in the South Pacific after the attack by the space battleship.</i>

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.740
<i>But the almighty submarine, Nautilus, is not defeated yet.</i>

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.340
Depth six hundred meters.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.300
How deep is the Kermodec Trench?

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.090
About ten thousand meters!

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.680
The depth usually means nothing,

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.100
but this time...

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:09.980
I wonder how we'll withstand it?

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.110
The Garfish fleet is approaching.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.410
A number of firing sounds! Depth charges coming!

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.170
The bombs struck the port bow! Water in the second living area!

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.800
The stern's interior has been damaged too!

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.720
Where are they?

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.760
Overhead, Sir! Distance is 1,800 meters!

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.890
I see. How is the compressed air?

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.600
Enough left for one more surfacing.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:56.280
Get everyone together in the main block.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.490
We'll strike with the combat block using our last buoyant force.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:00.530
Captain!

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:05.120
Self-destruction will be our only choice if we don't. Hurry up!

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:11.210
Yes, Sir! All crew, please come to the second shelter in the main block.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:16.210
Repeat! All crew, please assemble in the main block's second shelter.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.380
We're separating the combat block.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.220
What?

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.840
Can you hear me, Jean?

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.090
Yes...

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.810
I'm sorry about before.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.310
It's safe for you to stay there. Don't move.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.520
Ms. Electra!

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.360
Don't worry. You'll be okay.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:38.650
See you later.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.080
Separation of the third block is complete.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.160
Power source switched!

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:55.000
The combat block is functioning independently.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.340
Detonation is set for a depth of 800 meters.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.380
Distance is 1,500 meters. Everything is ready.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.090
Release the combat block!

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:02.680
Yes, Sir!

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:33.290
Nautilus has separated into two parts at a depth of 2,400.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:36.670
We've done it! The water pressure has torn them in two!

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.250
No.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.960
They've just cut off the weakened part.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.800
Impossible!

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:48.260
Get the Garfish spread out quickly or they will be involved.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.720
Yes, Sir!

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.320
Garfish destroyed! Shockwave approaching.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.740
It's always awful to hear.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.250
It can happen to us anytime.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:18.330
Yes, the ship doesn't have any power left to float up.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.050
The Garfish fleet has been completely destroyed.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.180
I'm very sorry, Lord Gargoyle!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.600
Damn them!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.640
How badly is the Nautilus damaged?

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.060
Sir! That is not known yet.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.270
So tough.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.490
What happened?

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.320
What is it?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.790
It's a deep ocean current. Flowing southwest at six knots.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.500
I see.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.210
Will you see to it?

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.790
Yes, Sir.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.680
The Nautilus is at a depth of 4,000 meters.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.180
I'm sorry. We can't pick it up any longer.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.690
The Nautilus can't stand any more

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:24.480
even if its body is made of the super alloy, space titanium.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.150
They took extensive damage throughout.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.160
We cornered it, but we couldn't give it the final blow.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.580
Who is responsible for this?

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.200
I'm sorry, Sir!

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.420
Forget it. It's a pity we couldn't see the end of the Nautilus.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.920
We should report this to the Emperor.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:46.590
Yes, Sir!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.550
Emperor Neo!

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:58.060
We have a report from Gargoyle.

00:06:58.730 --> 00:06:59.890
Put it through.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:00.900
Yes, Sir!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.020
Good news, Emperor Neo!

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:11.610
The Nautilus lies ruined at a depth of 4,000 meters in the Kermodec Trench.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.240
I see. Very good.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:24.210
Sir! Would Your Majesty please help us retrieve the Blue Waters that belonged to Nemo and Nadia?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.050
I will.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.920
We're grateful, Your Majesty!

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:32.680
I will make a precise report after I return.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.550
I'll see you again.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.060
I see. Excellent work.

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.850
Excellency! Thank you very much.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.860
Nemo and Nadia have died.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:55.660
So much blood has been sacrificed for the Blue Water over 12,000 years.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.090
Main staff, please come up to the sub-bridge.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.880
I will give you instructions there.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:10.590
Yes, Sir.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.100
Here you go! Fetch!

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:24.940
Come with me.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.530
Hey! Where are we going?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.490
Hey, Nadia! Tell me!

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.990
Where are we going?

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:40.750
Wow!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.620
This is...

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:43.960
The Captain's cabin?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:45.420
Yes, it is.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.000
Why, Captain? You said nobody could come in here.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.840
This room will be separated from the main block.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.590
You should leave the ship.

00:08:57.220 --> 00:08:58.970
You can't mean that!

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.180
Without any technological knowledge you are useless on this ship.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:07.860
Captain! We'll do anything!
We'll help you! Just...

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:20.490
Jean, please look after Nadia.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.040
Captain!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.510
Captain! Captain!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:40.760
Hey! Me too! Please! Captain!

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.060
Okay.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.940
Aren't you afraid of me?

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:49.610
A little bit. But I love you a bit too.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.280
Jean, I want you to take care of her too.

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:04.120
Bye-bye! See you later!

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.250
Captain!

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.310
You're still here?

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:44.620
What was that?

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.370
A gunshot?

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.040
It's no good! It won't open!

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.790
This doesn't work, either!

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:59.380
My life ended thirteen years ago,

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:03.600
the day I threw away my name
and left my hometown.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:09.390
No... The day you destroyed our homeland!

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.180
Yes...

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:46.600
That light was the beginning of everything.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:50.270
The queen of Tartessos, she was your wife!

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:53.600
That light killed the queen!

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:02.530
The coup d'etat of Tartessos that began with the murder of the queen,

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:04.660
ended with the victory of the rebels.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.210
The leader of the rebels called himself Gargoyle.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:21.510
He changed the name of the kingdom to the Neo Atlantis Empire.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:34.270
He was supported by Emperor Neo

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:39.530
who wanted to revive the Tower of Babel, sealed since ancient times.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.080
After all the seals were broken,

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:51.500
the Tower of Babel regained its natural power.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:57.330
When Gargoyle tried to show its power as a destructive weapon,

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.300
the tragedy took place.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.890
Lightning ran over the ground.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:16.150
Fire and wind raged over our country for seven days.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.110
It was just like a sea of fire.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:26.660
The angry water and earth swallowed everything

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.120
as if to cover that hell.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.790
We couldn't find the city.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.180
NO!

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.320
My brother was dead!

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.330
I slept twice,

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.040
before I met a living soul.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.920
He was you.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:22.660
I was very grateful to the person who saved me.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:28.210
When I found out that it was love,

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.220
I was so happy.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.800
I was content.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.770
But then I happened to learn

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:45.060
exactly what I never wanted to hear!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:49.110
Are you really going to raise her?

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:52.950
We're going through hell.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:55.780
I've been prepared for it for five years now.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:59.910
We must fight against Gargoyle to the bloody death.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.250
You want to raise her

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:11.000
to make amends for what you did five years ago?

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:14.970
You destroyed the Tower of Babel with your own hands.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:20.930
That's true. But there was no other way.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.350
You had to pull the Blue Water out of the control device,

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:29.770
to stop the Tower of Babel from working and make it self-destruct.

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:33.990
She's a substitute for your dead daughter.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.450
That's not true!

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:41.990
She seized the chance to survive in that hell.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:48.580
I want to help her live as she likes.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:54.380
You'll let her come with us if she wishes to?

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:00.970
There are as many lives as there are men.

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:05.890
Man cannot live on hatred alone.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:09.690
I hated you. I wanted to kill you!

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:14.530
I understand why you had to destroy the Tower.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:19.490
If you hadn't, Gargoyle would have devastated the world years ago.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:23.790
But my father, my mother, my brother

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:27.620
and all the people who were killed must be wondering...

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.250
Nadia asked the same question.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.710
How can you go on living?

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:37.220
I believed you intended to kill Gargoyle and Emperor Neo,

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:40.430
and destroy Neo Atlantis!

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:44.640
I believed you would spend as much blood as needed in order to do so.

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:47.270
That was why I followed you!

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:50.480
Believing in you! Loving you!

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:57.690
I didn't care, even if I was just a substitute for the daughter you loved.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:00.530
I just wanted to stay near you.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:06.160
Yes, until your daughter, Nadia, appeared in front of us!

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:11.960
I was afraid Nadia would take your heart away from me,

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:15.340
but you didn't tell her you were her father.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:18.970
You kept burning with vengeful thoughts toward Neo Atlantis.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:22.300
You remained the man I loved.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:24.010
But...

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:25.760
But...

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:29.730
Why did you have to go back to being an ordinary father?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:33.690
Why didn't you stay the man I loved?

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:40.780
Goodbye, Captain Nemo.

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:42.820
No! Stop it!

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:45.120
Please don't shoot!

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:46.200
Never mind!

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:51.120
I knew about your hatred. Shoot me!

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:53.080
Yes!

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:05.470
One shot is enough to kill you.

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:08.810
I think so.

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:16.570
I want you to tell me. Why didn't you kill yourself with Gargoyle?

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:21.780
I couldn't make the same mistake.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:27.870
Mistake? You mean you killed your people and ruined your homeland?

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:31.460
Yes.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:40.920
I must make up for what I did before. I live only for that.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:45.010
Why didn't you scuttle yourself then?

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:46.180
Why?

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:51.430
For thirteen years you've helped me.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:54.100
I think of you as my own daughter.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.810
I couldn't have you involved in this.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.110
Electra, I couldn't do it because of you!

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.910
It's not fair to tell me that.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:21.800
I can't shoot you now.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.760
I'll use the last bullet for myself.

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:29.430
I'll give you back the life you gave to me!

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:42.360
Don't be careless with your life!

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:44.950
You must live and consider what you have to do!

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.910
Man cannot live on hatred alone.

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:59.920
Isn't that right, Captain?

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:19.520
Nadia! Live!

00:22:54.810 --> 00:22:56.350
Nadia...

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.270
King! Stop that!

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:27.420
Father...

00:23:32.550 --> 00:23:34.180
Nadia...
